From 7a21a783cc888c745337ac2ed7026fbecefa467e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JohnnyC96 <54557697+JohnnyC96@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 16:10:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 60/61] Runtime: optional external IPU (MPEG-2 decoder) with
 DMA channels 3/4; PS2X_IPU=pcsx2|off from the external library

ps2_ipu_external.h: ps2x::IpuDevice, setIpuDevice, ps2CreateExternalIpu (PS2X_EXTERNAL_GS). When one is installed,
PS2Memory routes the IPU registers (CMD/CTRL writes; 64-bit halves, BP and TOP read-only), the FIFOs (IPU_in
assembled from four word writes, IPU_out pulled on the first word; read128 too) and the channel 3/4 registers to it,
reads IPU registers through it in read64 (libipu reads IPU_CMD/IPU_TOP with ld), and mirrors D_CTRL.DMAE and the
D_ENABLEW suspend bit. advanceEeTimers advances it on the EE cycle count and returns its INTC cause 8 (bit 8) and the
end of channel 3/4 (D_STAT 3/4 set, causes queued; bit 31); cyclesUntilNextEeTimerInterrupt includes its next event;
EeScheduler::processPendingEvents dispatches cause 8 and drains the queued DMAC handlers. Created after memory init.
No header seen by generated code changes. Resident Evil Outbreak's movies run Sony's libmpeg/libipu on it.

Test: PS2Memory "an external IPU gets its registers, FIFOs, channels 3/4 and DMAC state, and its events raise
interrupts" (fake device).
